## 65. člen

(1)	When imposing a measure of protective supervision, the court may also order one or more instructions which the convicted person must follow.
(2)	In selecting the instructions, the court shall take into account in particular the offender's age, his mental characteristics, the motives from which he committed the act, personal circumstances, his previous life,

the circumstances in which he committed the act, and his behaviour after the commission of the criminal offence. It must take special care that the choice of instructions does not violate the convicted person's human dignity or cause him particular difficulties.
(3)	The court's instructions may include the following tasks:
1)	treatment in an appropriate health institution, with consent also treatment for alcohol or drug addiction;
2)	attendance at an appropriate vocational, psychological or other counselling service;
3)	training for a profession or acceptance of employment that corresponds to the convicted person's health, abilities and inclination;
4)	use of income in accordance with maintenance obligations;
5)	prohibition of association with certain persons;
6)	prohibition of establishing direct or indirect contact with one or more specified persons, including by use of electronic means of communication;
7)	prohibition of approaching the victim or any other persons;
8)	prohibition of access to individual places;
9)	inclusion in one or more social welfare services of the social work centre.
(4)	During the probationary period, the court may modify or revoke the instructions ex officio, on the proposal of the counsellor or the convicted person.

Activity of the counsellor

## 66. člen

(1)	Protective supervision is carried out by a counsellor appointed by the authority responsible for
probation.
(2)	The counsellor provides assistance and protection to the convicted person in accordance with the law governing probation and supervises the fulfilment of the instructions issued by the court to the convicted person.

Consequences of non-compliance with instructions

## 67. člen

(1)	If the convicted person does not comply with the instructions during the probationary period, evades contact with the counsellor or otherwise breaches the personal plan prepared in accordance with the law governing probation, the court may warn him, modify the instructions, extend the protective supervision beyond the limit of the specified probationary period for the time of non-compliance with the instructions, evasion of contact or other breach of the personal plan, or revoke the suspended sentence and impose the sentence that was specified in the suspended sentence.
(2)	If the convicted person also during the extended protective supervision from the previous paragraph does not comply with the instructions, evades contact with the counsellor or otherwise breaches the personal plan prepared in accordance with the law governing probation, the court may revoke the suspended sentence and impose the sentence that was specified in the suspended sentence.

3.	Judicial admonition

Conditions for imposing a judicial admonition

## 68. člen

(1)	A judicial admonition may be imposed for criminal offences for which a fine or imprisonment of up to one year is prescribed, if they are committed in such mitigating circumstances as to make them particularly minor.
(2)	For certain criminal offences, a judicial admonition may be imposed under the conditions specified by law, even when imprisonment of up to three years is prescribed for them.
(3)	The court may impose a judicial admonition for several criminal offences committed in concurrence, if the conditions from the first or second paragraph of this article are met for each of these offences.
(4)	In deciding whether to impose a judicial admonition, the court shall take into account the personality of the offender, his previous life, his behaviour after the commission of the criminal offence, the degree of guilt and other circumstances in which the act was committed.
(5)	For an offender who, under the law governing criminal procedure, admits guilt when first making a statement on the indictment in which the imposition of a judicial admonition is proposed for such a case, or admits it in an agreement with the state prosecutor, the court may impose a judicial admonition also for criminal offences for which imprisonment of up to three years is prescribed.

Sixth Chapter SECURITY MEASURES

Types of security measures

## 69. člen

The following security measures may be imposed on perpetrators of criminal offences:
1)	mandatory psychiatric treatment and custody in a health institution;
2)	mandatory psychiatric treatment at liberty;
3)	prohibition of practising a profession;
4)	prohibition of approaching or communicating with the victim;
5)	revocation of driving licence;
6)	confiscation of objects.

Imposition of security measures

